        rules: {
          objective: 'Win the final trick of the hand. If you win it with a 7, you score higher bonus points.',
          gameplay: '1. Players must follow suit if possible.\n2. Highest card of the suit led wins the trick.\n3. Winner of a trick leads the next.\n4. **The Last Trick**: Only the points from the last one, two, or three tricks matter.',
          keyRules: [
            'Must follow suit if possible; if void, play any card.',
            'Highest card of the suit led wins the trick; winner leads the next trick.',
            'Only the last one, two, or three tricks are scored; winning the last trick with a 7 scores 2 points, with another card 1 point; winning the last two tricks with 7s scores 4 points; all three last tricks with 7s scores 6 points.',
            'First to reach agreed target (e.g. 10 points) wins; winner of each hand deals the next.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Save your high cards (Aces, Kings) to win control of the lead in the mid-game, then lead your 7s in the final tricks when everyone else has run out of higher cards of that suit.',
          intermediate: "Suit tracking: Pay close attention to which suits have been 'voided' by other players. If you know the person to your left is out of Diamonds, your Diamond-7 becomes a guaranteed point if you have the lead for the last trick.",
          advanced: "Defensive Lead: If you don't have a 7, lead your highest card for the final trick to prevent an opponent from winning with their 7.",
          tips: [
            "The '7' is the most valuable card in the game. Don't waste it on a middle trick.",
            'If you see someone hoarding cards of a single suit, try to force that suit out early.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
